+### Target folder
+
+`targets/<id>/` separates OS-specific data from the shared procedure in
+[policy-gate/v1](../specs/policy-gate/v1.md). Ubuntu 26.04 (`ubuntu-26.04`) is
+the first and currently only target; bash remains the only supported shell.
+
+- REPL start-up reads `target.toml`, selecting exact os-release `ID` and
+  `VERSION_ID`; no `ID_LIKE` or nearby-version fallback. A user-named target
+  (`--target` or config) is required without a match. A mismatched named target
+  requires confirmation for every command.
+- The gate uses the target's package-owner query, sensitive locations and, as
+  planned, `allowlist.toml`; gate tests read `gate-vectors.toml`.
+- The REPL and reader load command and reader prompt pieces from `prompts/`;
+  training also consumes the target's prompts.
+- The installer will read `model.toml` for weight downloads and verification;
+  the REPL will check those hashes before loading (section 7).
+- The pipeline will read `harvest.toml` for harvest configuration and VM image,
+  and `eval/` for the frozen split and OS probes used by training and release.
+
+Intended runtime files are `target.toml`, `model.toml`, `allowlist.toml`,
+`sensitive.toml` and `prompts/`; `gate-vectors.toml` is test data.
+`harvest.toml` and `eval/` are build-time material, not runtime requirements.
+
